Z||000000||GT Bastard||05-16-2000||04:11 PM||||Well, I finally got the nerve to start dismantling the top-end of my motor today(rebuilding and porting heads, porting and fixing exhaust manifolds.)I'm down to removing the head bolts, but I need to get a breaker bar.  It all came apart pretty easily, but it's a little unsettling to see the intake, fuel rail, injectors, pushrods, etc sitting on my garage floor! So far, nothing shows any signs of wear.  Pushrods look brand spankin' new, and everything is reletively clean. This sh*t is fun man!!! I've gotta tear my car apart more often.  In fact, tonight I'm picking up everything I need to do my auto to manual swap for 200 bucks.  Yeeeeeehaawwwww.  <P>Anybody know how much a used set of 3.1 injectors go for?||||reg||11
Z||000001||mshill||05-16-2000||06:12 PM||||I felt the same way when my 86SE V6 engine was up on the stand.  It is even better when it is all back together, and you crank it for the first time and it starts right up.<P>Just getting ready to dig into the top end on my 86GT as well.  I love this stuff.<P>||||reg||10
